# Local override for this client surface's dev server. Copy to .env (gitignored).
#
# BOTH ARE OPTIONAL. Leave them unset and the app dials the origin it was served
# from for the bff (/memql/ws, proxied by Vite in dev and by the app.<domain>
# Ingress in a cluster), which is what a client surface should do -- it removes
# a whole class of CORS and mis-pointing bugs, and it is why the bff's
# MEMQL_SERVER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS can stay a concrete, non-wildcard value.
#
# Set VITE_MEMQL_HTTP_URL only when the SPA really is served from a DIFFERENT
# origin than the bff. Do NOT point it at bff.<domain> in a cloud install: that
# host is the RAW gRPC ingress (backend-protocol GRPC, :50051), so a browser
# WebSocket upgrade sent there hands HTTP/1.1 to an h2c backend and fails with a
# protocol error naming nothing.
# VITE_MEMQL_HTTP_URL=

# The identity service base URL. Only /auth/magic-link needs it -- the front
# door proxies /oauth/token, /auth/refresh, /auth/logout and the JWKS feed
# same-origin -- and it defaults to https://identity.__DOMAIN__.
# VITE_IDENTITY_BASE_URL=https://identity.__DOMAIN__
